@startuml 02_sequence_diagram
title FairCreditScore — Five End-to-End Workflows

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam SequenceMessageAlignment center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1565C0

actor Customer
actor Ops
actor Lender
participant "Browser\n(Templates)" as UI
participant "Django Views\n(core.views)" as Views
participant "Scoring Engine\n(core.scoring)" as Scoring
participant "ORM" as ORM
database "DB" as DB

== 1. Customer signs up ==
Customer -> UI : GET /signup/
UI -> Views : signup()
Views -> ORM : create User + CustomerProfile
ORM -> DB : INSERT
Views --> UI : 302 → /me/
UI --> Customer : Dashboard

== 2. Document upload ==
Customer -> UI : POST /me/documents/upload/
UI -> Views : upload_document()
Views -> Views : DocumentUploadForm.clean_file\n(MIME, ≤10MB)
Views -> ORM : Document(status=uploaded)
ORM -> DB : INSERT
Views -> ORM : AuditLog(action=document_upload)
Views --> UI : 302 → /me/

== 3. AA consent (mock) ==
Customer -> UI : POST /me/consent/initiate/
UI -> Views : initiate_consent()
Views -> Views : secrets.token_hex(16)
Views -> ORM : AAConsent(status=pending)
Views --> UI : 302 → /me/consent/<handle>/
Customer -> UI : POST /me/consent/<handle>/approve/
UI -> Views : consent_approve()
Views -> ORM : status=active, approved_at=now()

== 4. Score generation (canonical) ==
Customer -> UI : POST /me/score/generate/\n(algorithm=canonical)
UI -> Views : generate_my_score()
Views -> Scoring : generate_score(user, "canonical")
Scoring -> Scoring : _generate_features(seeded RNG)
Scoring -> Scoring : _to_subscores(...) → 0..100
Scoring -> Scoring : alt = Σ subscore × weight
Scoring -> Scoring : score = round(300 + alt × 6)
Scoring -> ORM : ScoreReport(...)
ORM -> DB : INSERT
Views --> UI : 302 → /me/score/<id>/
UI --> Customer : Dial + SHAP-style factors

== 5. Lender API ==
Lender -> Views : GET /api/lender/score/<customer_id>/
Views -> ORM : ScoreReport.objects.filter(customer=...).first()
ORM -> DB : SELECT
Views --> Lender : 200 JSON {score, band, factors, ...}

@enduml
